// Tessera stdlib: the correctly rounded complementary error function of F64
//
// For x < 0x1.713786d9c7c09p+1 (and negative x) erfc(x) = 1 - erf(x) from the
// double-double erf kernels of erf.tess; above, the asymptotic form
// erfc(x) = exp(-x^2) p(1/x) with a double-double exp and odd polynomials in
// 1/x from tables. A fast path with an absolute error bound decides most
// inputs; the rest go through an accurate path of about 104 bits, with
// CORE-MATH's hard-to-round inputs answered from tables, and a careful final
// scaling for subnormal results. Round to nearest only: -inf gives 2, +inf
// gives +0, NaN comes back quiet; erfc(x) rounds to 0 for
// x >= 0x1.b39dc41e48bfdp+4.
//
// Ported from CORE-MATH, src/binary64/erfc/erfc.c via RazorForge's B64Erfc.rf.
// Copyright (c) 2022-2026 Alexei Sibidanov, Paul Zimmermann, Tom Hubrecht and
// Claude-Pierre Jeannerod
// MIT license: see LICENSE-CORE-MATH

module Standard::Core

